          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On December 6, 2024, in the evening, a witness observing the sky from their home in Pontivy (56) notices a stationary bright point. Shortly after, four similar sources appear. These objects suddenly start moving rapidly, accompanied by light trails (described as \"flames\") before disappearing. During a second observation sequence, the witness notes three bright points moving very quickly with marked acceleration, followed by the appearance of several white objects performing maneuvers of clustering and dispersion. The witness suggests it could be a flock of gulls. Of average strangeness and low consistency* due to only one witness, and despite attempts to obtain additional information, including photos/videos that could have been captured with a smartphone, this case could not be analyzed. *According to the criteria of GEIPAN, consistency is the amount of reliable and objective information gathered for a testimony. The GEIPAN classifies the case as \"C\", unidentified phenomenon due to lack of data.",
